# DAX Measures

This file contains the primary DAX measures used in the Executive Sales Dashboard.

---

Measure 1: Total Revenue

Calculates total sales revenue.

Total Revenue =
SUMX(
    Sales,
    Sales[Quantity] * Sales[Unit Price]
)

---
  
Measure 2: Total Orders

Calculates the number of unique orders.

Total Orders =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[Order ID])

---
Measure 3: Total Customers

Calculates the number of unique customers.
  
Total Customers =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[Customer ID])

  
---

Measure 4: Total Units Sold

Calculates the total quantity of products sold.
  Total Units Sold =
SUM(Sales[Quantity])

---

Measure 5: Average Order Value

Calculates average revenue generated per order.
  Average Order Value =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue],
    [Total Orders],
    0
)

---

Measure 6: Previous Year Revenue

Calculates total revenue for the previous year.
  Previous Year Revenue =
CALCULATE(
    [Total Revenue],
    SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR('Date'[Date])
)

---
Measure 7: Revenue Year-over-Year Growth

Calculates the percentage change in revenue compared with the previous year.
Revenue YoY Growth % =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue] - [Previous Year Revenue],
    [Previous Year Revenue],
    0
)
  
  
